+
+## Selected configuration coverage
+
+Every harness invocation re-reads [`_tests-RobustModem.md`](../_tests-RobustModem.md),
+records its SHA-256 and preserves repeated rows. Malformed or incomplete rows
+fail rather than silently omitting a case. Its `configuration_inventory` provides
+nominal total DATA and Helper power/noise density for each row using the native
+exporter's -164 dBm/Hz assumption, with the native default 90 dB Helper/DATA
+power ratio ceiling. This is arithmetic, not a sampled channel or reception
+measurement. A zero Helper is reported as absent. Changing the noise density or
+physical model changes the numbers; they are not a target for success.
+
+**None of the listed cases is yet simulated by this harness.** Each inventory
+row explicitly marks all requested case-level outcomes unimplemented. The kernel
+measurements above use a separate synthetic fixture and cannot establish case
+CPU seconds per received second, DSP workspace margin, success probability or
+SNR target, single-bit or `fox` transmission time, or preparation requirements.
+The Python acquisition and tracking stages are not integrated; the weak receiver
+requires usable Helper, so Helper-off cases need additional acquisition work.
+The native exporter accepts bounded single-bit streams; whole-message reception
+and a faithful mapping from every listed setting remain to be implemented.
+Do not interpret a successful kernel run as completing this configuration suite.
+
+To extend it, first establish a faithful source/channel/receiver path for each
+selected stratum, including the no-Helper cases, specified impairments and
+message framing. Predeclare small statistical samples and stopping rules for
+success separately from timing. Measure post-preparation CPU and elapsed time
+for representative steady processing, including all receiver stages, and compare
+the actual allocation and workspace with the computer's ceiling; account for
+all threads and do not substitute a single kernel projection. Record noise,
+source/configuration hashes, seeds, message and preparation calendar, and the
+uncertainty and applicability of any extrapolation. Report unresolved cases
+instead of substituting an unrelated fixture or ideal detector forecast.
+
+For the current unfinished configuration-coverage investigation, the local
+`local-evidence/triad-abbreviated.json` and `local-evidence/score-only-cpu.json`
+record the abbreviated fixture observations, and `local-evidence/cpu_fixture.py`
+reproduces the separate process-CPU check. Remove these when the question is
+resolved or replaced by current configuration-specific evidence. The local
+build tree supports the same investigation; retire it when no longer used.
